From 1c21695283572ebc51145565bac327fe4e57bd1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 349/488] soh: name the 17 address-named symbols defined in
 z_vr_box.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 17 are defined in soh/src/code/z_vr_box.c.

  * D_8012AC90 -> sRoomFaceTexOffsets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the four 0x10000-step texture offsets, one per
    face of a room skybox.

  * D_8012ACA0 -> sRoomVtxIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: two 0x20-entry index lists picking which of
    the generated vertices each room-skybox face uses.

  * D_8012AD20 -> sRoomVtxU
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the five texture U coordinates a room-skybox
    face's vertices are laid out on.

  * D_8012AD2C -> sRoomVtxV
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the nine texture V coordinates for the same
    grid.

  * D_8012AD40 -> sRoomQuadIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the 0x40 vertex indices, four per quad, that
    stitch a room-skybox face into sixteen quads.

  * D_8012ADC0 -> sSkyFaceTexOffsets
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the six 0x2000-step texture offsets, one per
    face of the outdoor skybox.

  * D_8012ADD8 -> sSkyVtxIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the 0x20 vertex indices used by each
    outdoor-skybox face.

  * D_8012AE18 -> sSkyVtxU
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the five texture U coordinates for an
    outdoor-skybox face.

  * D_8012AE24 -> sSkyVtxV
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the five texture V coordinates for the four
    side faces.

  * D_8012AE30 -> sSkyVtxVCap
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the V coordinates for the top and bottom
    faces, which fold back on themselves so the texture meets at the pole.

  * D_8012AE3C -> sSkyQuadIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the 0x40 vertex indices, four per quad, that
    stitch an outdoor-skybox face into sixteen quads.

  * D_8012AEBC -> sRoomFaceParams
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the four room-skybox faces, each carrying the
    five parameters the room face builder needs.

  * D_8012AF0C -> sSkyFaceParams
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the six outdoor-skybox faces, each carrying
    the five parameters the sky face builder needs.

  * func_800ADBB0 -> Skybox_BuildRoomFace
    deduced, confidence HIGH: generates the vertices and quads of one
    room-skybox face into roomVtx and the display list buffer, returning the
    next free vertex index.

  * func_800AE2C0 -> Skybox_BuildSkyFace
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the outdoor-skybox twin: it generates one
    face's vertices and quads and returns the next free vertex index.

  * func_800AEFC8 -> Skybox_BuildRoom
    deduced, confidence HIGH: builds the whole room skybox, using two faces
    for the shops, three for one special case and four otherwise.

  * func_800AF178 -> Skybox_BuildSky
    deduced, confidence HIGH: builds the requested number of outdoor-skybox
    faces, five for the ordinary sky and six for the cutscene map.

